    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lean on the premium matchup quality of **Gunnar Henderson** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** today, as both anchor our offense despite facing tough right-handed opposition. **Gunnar Henderson** (74.74) remains a must-start; while Gerrit Cole\u2019s elite skill profile creates a drag on his score, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from an aggressive +16% park adjustment and his prime #3 spot. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) is our highest-projected hitter against Kyle Bradish, with a +16% park boost and the likelihood of hitting third maximizing his potential for counting stats. **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) also earns a strong recommendation, as his leadoff role against the vulnerable G. Holmes is a key driver for Roto category gains, particularly in speed-starved rosters.\n\nThe optimizer faced a difficult choice regarding **Wade Meckler** (48.71) and **Coby Mayo** (45.87), both of whom hold marginal scores but remain in the lineup to avoid wasted game caps. **Nasim Nunez** (36.77) was the closest exclusion from the starting nine; while **Nasim Nunez** provides high-end SB utility, his matchup against a high-tier arm like Jacob deGrom and a suppressed #9 spot in the batting order pushed his efficiency score well below the starting threshold. We are monitoring lineup confirmations for **Heliot Ramos**, whose score of 64.74 is tempered slightly by the opposing pitcher\u2019s ability to control the run game, but he remains a high-floor start given the projected environment.\n\nInvestors should remain wary of the volatility surrounding **Coby Mayo** and **Wade Meckler**, as their statuses are dependent on official lineup releases. With **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Jackson Merrill** currently unavailable due to injury or scheduling, the burden of production rests on our top-tier trio of **Gunnar Henderson**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, and **Sam Antonacci**. We are keeping a close watch on **Miguel Vargas** (59.39) as well; he sits just shy of the \"Strong\" start threshold but remains a viable play against Holmes due to a favorable xwOBA. If any late weather developments surface in the venues hosting **Heliot Ramos** or **Drake Baldwin**, we will pivot to maintain our efficiency targets.",
